{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AJGrEKurdMnGDfJikgBTWd","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"960f1cb95496e66ab8047a5f83eda6c1b2ecb2e2","date":"2026-08-15T02:00:17+05:30","message":"TRUNK-6717: Replace reflective BeanUtils property access with direct PersonName getters (#6431)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ranidu Nethma","authorEmail":"113999336+RaniduNethma@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"73c69ec0cea55efa51d67a8d3f19899c6eb5cf93","date":"2026-08-14T12:44:58-07:00","message":"TRUNK-6758: Remove MigrationHelper (#6457)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Idontknowthough","authorEmail":"tomlu60220244@gmail.com"},{"hash":"05bc4e4dc32c4654aba49cc76b9252def11b06c2","date":"2026-08-14T20:37:23+05:30","message":"TRUNK-6680: Restore lazy fetch semantics after JPA migration (#6379)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Mahesh5f4","authorEmail":"167050186+Mahesh5f4@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"8bb5c2e9e36ab8fb09f0053786bc0f040775cc1e","date":"2026-08-11T20:49:53+05:30","message":"TRUNK-6733: Use java-uuid-generator for entity UUIDs instead of UUID.randomUUID() (#6391)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Sathieskumar Sudeshkar","authorEmail":"sudeshkar008sk@gmail.com"},{"hash":"1b5421a9a8d69030adb91124c3f9cb758dbc58a8","date":"2026-07-24T11:14:02-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6712: Cache flattened role privileges for privilege and superuser checks (#6383)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"befcc055a108c28458fc21ff73f07dfe844f78a4","date":"2026-07-24T10:16:21-04:00","message":"Improve test suite run time (#6377)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"20b5abcfcfd8c73e0fbe40ea4586280bfff8f61e","date":"2026-07-23T13:40:47+03:00","message":"maven(deps): bump hibernateVersion from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final (#6309)","refs":"","body":"* maven(deps): bump hibernateVersion from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\n\nBumps `hibernateVersion` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final.\n\nUpdates `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-core` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/blob/7.4.5/changelog.txt)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/compare/7.3.6...7.4.5)\n\nUpdates `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-c3p0` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/blob/7.4.5/changelog.txt)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/compare/7.3.6...7.4.5)\n\nUpdates `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-envers` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/blob/7.4.5/changelog.txt)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/compare/7.3.6...7.4.5)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-core\n  dependency-version: 7.4.5.Final\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n- dependency-name: org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-c3p0\n  dependency-version: 7.4.5.Final\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n- dependency-name: org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-envers\n  dependency-version: 7.4.5.Final\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* Restore primary key on order_type_class_map join table for Hibernate 7.4\n\nHibernate ORM 7.4 changed set-collection DDL generation: when a Set-based\n@ManyToMany join table declares an explicit @UniqueConstraint covering all\nof its columns, Hibernate now emits that unique constraint in place of the\ncomposite primary key it previously generated. OrderType.conceptClasses was\nthe only join table carrying such a constraint, so order_type_class_map was\ncreated without a primary key.\n\nNon-transactional integration tests build the schema via hbm2ddl and load\nstandardTestDataset.xml with dbunit's REFRESH operation, which requires a\nprimary key, so every one of them failed in setup with\nNoPrimaryKeyException: ORDER_TYPE_CLASS_MAP.\n\nThe Set's composite key already enforces the exact uniqueness the annotation\ndeclared, making uniqueConstraints redundant, and the production schema is\ndefined by Liquibase (unaffected). Removing it restores the composite primary\nkey and makes order_type_class_map consistent with the other @ManyToMany join\ntables (user_role, location_tag_map, concept_name_tag_map).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dependabot[bot]","authorEmail":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"1f6cc621cb7bf97dc4283b0c808f96373d90054f","date":"2026-07-22T15:41:22-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6711: Batch-load search result pages (#6363)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"9e011e2c09db99fd5cae20821e203fe9cc5f036b","date":"2026-07-21T23:50:01+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6681: Improve LocationSearchCriteria query performance with pagination (#6359)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"omeri innocent","authorEmail":"innocentomeri08@gmail.com"},{"hash":"265582974b2589ffc8787b57c2e4ba0368cb6cba","date":"2026-07-21T12:44:21-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6713: Follow-up: Comment clean-up","refs":"","body":"This was already included in the backports\n","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b68355b3dd934c7d5be3708d6637dfae8f845ee5","date":"2026-07-21T11:26:59-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6713: Switch to saner DaemonThread protection scheme (#6349)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"41ec2955656c6d7131c628d122d8c503b09c4cb1","date":"2026-07-21T10:37:09-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6694 & TRUNK-6695: Avoid synchronization in service fetching (#6348)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"50810cfb4d919602fa727eb78607675e2a5e3ec0","date":"2026-07-21T01:25:50+03:00","message":"Require Get Patient Programs privilege for by-uuid program lookups (#6318)","refs":"","body":"* Require Get Patient Programs privilege for by-uuid program lookups\n\nProgramWorkflowService.getPatientProgramByUuid and getPatientStateByUuid\nhad no @Authorized annotation. Because AuthorizationAdvice only enforces\nwhen a method declares a privilege, both fell through with no check at\nall, letting any authenticated user read program-enrollment PHI by uuid.\nEvery other read on the service, including getPatientProgram(Integer),\nalready requires Get Patient Programs; annotate both by-uuid methods to\nmatch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Require Get Patient Programs privilege for patient program attribute lookup\n\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName returns patient program\nattribute values keyed by patient id, yet lacked an @Authorized check.\nIts two sibling attribute readers (getPatientProgramAttributeByUuid and\ngetPatientProgramByAttributeNameAndValue) already guard on Get Patient\nPrograms, so this was a missed PHI read of the same class addressed by\nGHSA-gqf9-38mg-wgqg.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\n\n* Add authorization tests pinning the by-uuid program privilege checks\n\nThe existing tests for getPatientProgramByUuid, getPatientStateByUuid and\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName run as the privileged superuser\nand assert only find/null behavior, so they pass even if the\n@Authorized(Get Patient Programs) checks added by this branch are removed.\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName had no test at all.\n\nAdd a test per method that logs out (dropping Get Patient Programs) and\nasserts APIAuthenticationException is thrown for otherwise-valid arguments,\nmirroring AuthorizationAdviceTest and AdministrationServiceTest. These fail\nif any of the three annotations is removed, pinning the fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"f46e57d17c70440830a6ef07fde6296a79f5aed6","date":"2026-07-21T00:49:11+03:00","message":"Require allergy privileges for getAllergies and setAllergies (#6324)","refs":"","body":"* Require allergy privileges for getAllergies and setAllergies\n\nPatientService.getAllergies(Patient) and setAllergies(Patient, Allergies)\ncarried no @Authorized annotation. AuthorizationAdvice only enforces when\na method declares a privilege, so both fell through with no check at all,\nletting any authenticated caller read or modify any patient's allergy\nlist. The per-item siblings are already guarded (getAllergy and\ngetAllergyByUuid require Get Allergies; saveAllergy requires Add/Edit\nAllergies). Annotate getAllergies with Get Allergies and setAllergies with\nAdd/Edit Allergies, and add regression tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Do not transitively require Get Allergies for internal allergy reads\n\nPR #6324 added @Authorized(GET_ALLERGIES) to PatientService.getAllergies.\nTwo internal callers reach getAllergies through the AOP service proxy, so\nthey now transitively demand Get Allergies from the outer caller. This is a\nbehavior change the existing tests did not catch:\n\n- AllergyValidator reads the patient's existing allergies to reject a\n  duplicate allergen whenever a new allergy is saved (allergyId == null).\n  That runs inside saveAllergy (RequiredDataAdvice -> ValidateUtil.validate\n  -> AllergyValidator) and on the encounter-save path, so a user holding\n  only Add/Edit Allergies could no longer add an allergy.\n- PatientServiceImpl.mergeAllergies reads both patients' allergies, but\n  mergePatients is only @Authorized(EDIT_PATIENTS), so merging began to\n  require Get Allergies as well.\n\nWrap each internal read in the standard addProxyPrivilege /\nremoveProxyPrivilege idiom so the read is done on the caller's behalf\nwithout forcing the outer operation to hold Get Allergies. The interface\n@Authorized on getAllergies is left unchanged, so direct reads still\nrequire the privilege.\n\nAdd a revert-sensitive PatientServiceTest that saves a new allergy as a\nuser holding only Add Allergies (not Get Allergies); without the fix it\nfails with an APIAuthenticationException for Get Allergies raised from the\nvalidator's duplicate check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\n\n* Run the merge workflow tests as a non-super user\n\nmergeAndRetrieveAudit now executes mergePatients as a user who holds\nonly the privileges the merge legitimately requires, with Get Allergies\ndeliberately absent, so every audit-based merge workflow test guards the\nGet Allergies proxy block in mergeAllergies: removing that block fails\nall 27 of them with \"Privileges required: Get Allergies\".\n\nRunning the merge without super-user privileges surfaced one more\ninternal read that leaked its privilege onto the caller: voiding the\nlosing patient triggers PatientDataVoidHandler, which proxies Edit\nCohorts for CohortService.notifyPatientVoided, but the membership read\ninside that method goes through the service proxy and demanded Get\nPatient Cohorts from the voiding user. That read now acquires its own\nproxy privilege, matching the allergy reads, and the test privilege set\nomits Get Patient Cohorts so both internal reads stay covered.\n\nSuggested by @ibacher during review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"d992f1746c140dc2effaf78fc86443ac35309a3c","date":"2026-07-20T23:48:04+03:00","message":"Bind caller-supplied names as query parameters instead of concatenating (#6335)","refs":"","body":"* Bind the program-attribute name as a query parameter\n\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName assembled its native query by\nconcatenating the attributeName argument straight into the SQL text. Bind\nit as a named parameter (:attributeName) instead so the value is always\nhandled as a literal attribute-type name and can never alter the query.\nThe patient-id list stays inlined since those elements are ints.\n\nAdds a regression test that a name containing SQL control characters is\nmatched literally and resolves no attribute type.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\n\n* Bind the global-property name in FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue\n\nReplace the concatenated global_property lookup with a PreparedStatement\nso the property name is always treated as a literal value rather than\nbeing spliced into the SQL text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add regression test for FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue name binding\n\nGuards that the property name is matched literally: a name carrying SQL\ncontrol characters resolves no property (returns null) instead of being\ninterpreted as query text, which the earlier concatenated query allowed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"c21a7cbfa2c9f67c1991372a343217e949e04f44","date":"2026-07-17T18:15:32-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6683: Skip full-text search with drugs when a concept is provided (#6346)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"375abbe5b5f9a52df6ea4cce33fc3ecdfba16c77","date":"2026-07-17T16:35:27-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6516: Follow-up: fix tests","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"11489bdb02063ff8138f45803c336b7ef4635179","date":"2026-07-17T08:26:55-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6687: Improve performance of searches using the search index (#6342)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"eb0a1006c7e188d4408deb298685c98ea1fef321","date":"2026-07-17T07:59:02-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6688: Fix circular initialization error in logging setup (#6341)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"d8fe1365fbce0b4d3fc43045dff3b69ce58ca2f4","date":"2026-07-15T16:25:59+03:00","message":"Require privileges for unprotected CohortService methods (#6317)","refs":"","body":"* Require Purge Cohorts privilege for CohortService.purgeCohort\n\npurgeCohort permanently and irreversibly removes a cohort from the\ndatabase but carried no @Authorized annotation, so any authenticated\nuser could reach it through the REST purge path\n(DELETE /ws/rest/v1/cohort/{uuid}?purge=true), even though the\nreversible voidCohort on the same resource requires Delete Cohorts.\nA dedicated Purge Cohorts privilege already exists in PrivilegeConstants\nbut was never applied. Annotate purgeCohort with it, consistent with the\nrest of the service.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add regression test for Purge Cohorts authorization\n\nGuards the @Authorized gate on CohortService.purgeCohort so that\ndropping the annotation fails the build instead of silently\nreopening the purge path to unprivileged callers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Require Get Patient Cohorts privilege for CohortService.getCohorts\n\ngetCohorts(String) was the only read on the service with no\n@Authorized, reading straight from the DAO while every sibling\ngetter requires Get Patient Cohorts. A direct service-layer caller\ncould therefore list cohorts (names, descriptions, member patient\nids) with no authorization; the REST search path was only covered\nincidentally by the resource's required-get privilege at conversion\ntime. Gate it at the service layer to match the other getters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Assert the specific privilege in cohort authorization tests\n\nCapture the thrown APIAuthenticationException and assert its message\nnames the required privilege, so a future edit that swaps either\nannotation to a different privilege (for purgeCohort, the exact\nregression this PR fixes: gating on Get Patient Cohorts instead of\nPurge Cohorts) fails the build rather than staying green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Use containsString matcher for cohort authorization assertions\n\nassertThat(msg, containsString(privilege)) reports the actual message\non failure, so a future privilege regression is self-describing in the\nCI log instead of the bare \"expected true but was false\" that\nassertTrue(msg.contains(..)) produces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"9c515246b4f37eafec0d6fc24de5b0455b9e3951","date":"2026-07-15T02:38:10+03:00","message":"mergePatients does not reassign Conditions, Allergies, or MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient (#6198) (#6315)","refs":"","body":"* mergePatients now reassigns Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient\n\nPatientServiceImpl.mergePatients had no reassignment helpers for the\npatient-scoped Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses tables, which\nwere added to core after the merge logic was written. After a merge these\nclinical records stayed attached to the now-voided non-preferred patient and\nsilently disappeared from the surviving patient's record - a clinical-data-loss\nand patient-safety concern (e.g. a hidden allergy).\n\nAdd mergeConditions, mergeAllergies and mergeMedicationDispenses helpers that\nmove each non-voided record from the non-preferred to the preferred patient via\nthe corresponding services, mirroring the existing\nmergeObservationsNotContainedInEncounters pattern. Saving through the services\nkeeps the changes audited and emits the normal save events. The moves are\nrecorded in new PersonMergeLogData collections so they appear in the\nPersonMergeLog.\n\nAllergies are deduplicated by allergen: an allergy whose allergen the preferred\npatient already records is not moved, because a patient cannot hold two\nallergies for the same allergen and a duplicate would make the survivor's\nallergy list fail to load afterwards.\n\nFixes #6194\n\n\n\n* Keep @since on the new PersonMergeLogData accessors only, not the private fields\n\nThe moved* fields are private (not API and not rendered by Javadoc), so the\nfield-level @since 2.9.0 tags were redundant. The public getters/adders keep\n@since 2.9.0, matching the codebase convention (Patient, Condition, Allergy\nattach @since to accessors, not backing fields).\n\n\n\n---------\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit 51422097a51a0918a9524ce8c0bd3aa76d17e25a)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"a2d22b85955401c2d12d3ebecd9e3f483cd905e8","date":"2026-07-15T01:34:15+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6675: Module is not updated when omod changes (#6257) (#6314)","refs":"","body":"* TRUNK-6675: Module is not updated when omod changes\n\n* TRUNK-6675: Address review comments\n\n- Split the deleteDirectory try-catch in the optimized-startup branch so IOException from deletion logs an accurate message instead of \"Error while reading module last modified file\"\n- Pin getLibCacheFolderForModule_shouldRecreateNonEmptyDirWhenModuleChanged to the module-changed branch by explicitly setting optimized.startup=true\n\n\n\n* TRUNK-6675: Address review comments\n\n- Extract deleteLibCacheDir helper to reduce cognitive complexity (fixes SonarCloud quality gate)\n- Guard .moduleLastModified write on successful deletion so a failed delete does not mask the problem on the next restart\n- Fix Context.getRuntimeProperties() defensive-copy bug in both tests: mutate the copy and push it back via Context.setRuntimeProperties() so isOptimizedStartup() actually sees the change\n\n\n\n* Update api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/ModuleClassLoader.java\n\n\n\n---------\n\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit 918f05117302df56e7fb74193ffd4e4cf926d0ed)\n\nCo-authored-by: Rafal Korytkowski <rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"adec7344f655076c00cfa8ef033d998c2b8e1f5d","date":"2026-07-14T22:28:41+02:00","message":"TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6298)","refs":"","body":"* TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6289)\n\nAddresses findings 1, 2, 4, 5, 7 from the sign-off issue:\n\n- Finding 1: OutboxEventRegistry now triggers scheduler when listeners are\n  found, replacing the SmartInitializingSingleton in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer.\n  Adds registerBean() so modules can register listeners at runtime.\n- Finding 2: Use Context.loadClass() instead of Class.forName() in\n  OutboxPollingTaskHandler so module-defined event types resolve correctly.\n- Finding 4: Change outbox_event.payload and completed_listeners columns\n  from TEXT to MEDIUMTEXT in both the update changelog and schema-only snapshot;\n  align OutboxEvent entity columnDefinition to match.\n- Finding 5: BrokerEventListenerFactory now rejects BrokerIncomingEvent<?>\n  (wildcard/raw) at registration time with a clear error instead of silently\n  wiring a consumer that dead-letters every message.\n- Finding 7: Document on OpenmrsServiceEventAdvice that a synchronous\n  @EventListener exception aborting the service call is intentional.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix getMaximumPropertyLength to treat MEDIUMTEXT/TEXT/CLOB as unbounded\n\nOnly LONGTEXT was special-cased to return Integer.MAX_VALUE; MEDIUMTEXT\nand other LOB-like types fell through to column.getLength() (default 255),\ncausing ValidateUtil to reject payloads that fit the actual DB column.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix tests broken by Finding 1 and Finding 5 refactors\n\n- OutboxEventIT: afterSingletonsInstantiated() renamed to schedule()\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: raw BrokerIncomingEvent -> BrokerIncomingEvent<String>\n  to comply with the new fail-fast check for wildcard types\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix two test failures caused by Finding 4 and Finding 5 fixes\n\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: publish BrokerIncomingEvent<String> with a\n  payload so getResolvableType() resolves to the concrete generic type\n  and Spring's listener type-matching accepts it against the\n  BrokerIncomingEvent<String> method parameter.\n- HibernateAdministrationDAO: scope the MEDIUMTEXT/LONGTEXT unbounded\n  treatment to only those two explicit columnDefinition values; remove\n  CLOB since @Lob fields without columnDefinition map to CLOB in H2,\n  which would suppress the 64 KB TEXT length check in\n  BaseAttributeTypeValidatorTest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revise BrokerIncomingEvent/OutgoingEvent header docs and fix test\n\n* Address PR review comments on #6298\n\n- Restore deleteScheduledTasks() in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer and call\n  it from OutboxEventRegistry when disabled or no listeners found, so JobRunr\n  jobs don't keep firing after the last listener module is uninstalled\n- Drop registerBean(): ModuleUtil.refreshApplicationContext re-runs\n  afterSingletonsInstantiated() on module start, so module listeners are\n  picked up without any module-side call\n- Add String payloads to all three BrokerEventListenerTest events so\n  getResolvableType() resolves to BrokerIncomingEvent<String> and filter\n  tests actually exercise the source/broker filter logic\n- Add wildcard BrokerIncomingEvent<?> test case to BrokerEventListenerFactoryTest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"},{"hash":"17c7d2c4111bc928fd3d7bb90f6d767903ef032a","date":"2026-07-14T23:26:05+03:00","message":"Revert \"Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes (#6305)\" (#6312)","refs":"","body":"This reverts commit 4abaae2eebcf54375d5304d95a18c4b1e0a44cf7.","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"9533e285323873ae4ace289f2dfee0cd931d5622","date":"2026-07-14T23:05:24+03:00","message":"Clean up the module jar copy in ModuleClassLoader (#6307)","refs":"","body":"The module jar copy in getModuleUrls() managed its streams by hand and\nclosed them in a finally block that calls close() on references that are\nstill null when opening the input stream throws, relying on the\nsurrounding catch to swallow the resulting NullPointerException. Replace\nit with try-with-resources, which closes both streams in reverse order\nwith proper suppressed-exception handling and only closes the ones that\nwere actually opened.\n\nAlso drop the preceding \"if (!tmpModuleJar.exists()) createNewFile()\"\nblock: the FileOutputStream that copies into it creates the file anyway,\nso the pre-creation is redundant.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged; an IOException while copying is still caught and\nlogged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"4abaae2eebcf54375d5304d95a18c4b1e0a44cf7","date":"2026-07-14T23:04:43+03:00","message":"Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes (#6305)","refs":"","body":"* Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes\n\nModuleClassLoader.getLibCacheFolderForModule() wipes a module's lib cache\nfolder when the module file changed (or on non-optimized startup) so the\nmodule is fully re-expanded. It used File.delete(), which only removes an\nempty directory and silently no-ops on a populated one, and the return\nvalue was ignored. The cache folder always holds the module jar,\nlib/*.jar and the .moduleLastModified marker, so the delete never\nhappened.\n\nAs a result, any jar a module dropped between versions stayed in the\ncache and on the module classpath after an in-place upgrade, causing\nstale classes and version or class-identity conflicts that are hard to\ndiagnose because the omod on disk looks correct. Fresh installs are\nunaffected.\n\nReplace both delete sites with a recursive FileUtils.deleteDirectory()\nhelper, and harden the surrounding logic so a stale classpath cannot slip\nthrough silently:\n\n- If the .moduleLastModified marker cannot be read or parsed, we can no\n  longer tell whether the module changed, so clear the cache rather than\n  reuse it.\n- If the folder still cannot be fully cleared (for example a jar locked\n  by the OS during a hot reload), warn with an actionable message instead\n  of quietly expanding over the stale content.\n- Check the mkdirs() result so a cache folder that cannot be recreated is\n  visible rather than surfacing later as an obscure expansion failure.\n- Guard the recursive delete to a direct child of the lib cache root so a\n  malformed module id can never point it outside the cache.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Retry the lib cache prune on the next startup when it cannot complete\n\nTwo hardening changes to the recursive delete, from review:\n\n- getLibCacheFolderForModule no longer refreshes the .moduleLastModified\n  marker when the folder could not be fully cleared (e.g. jars still\n  locked by the previous classloader during a hot upgrade on Windows).\n  Stamping the new value over leftovers made every later optimized\n  startup trust the stale cache, so jars the delete failed to remove\n  would have stayed on the module classpath indefinitely; with a stale\n  or missing marker the next startup retries the delete once the locks\n  are gone and self-heals.\n\n- A stray regular file sitting at the cache folder's path is deleted\n  explicitly: FileUtils.deleteDirectory throws an unchecked\n  IllegalArgumentException for a non-directory, which would escape the\n  IOException catch and fail the module's startup, where the previous\n  File#delete() silently recovered.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Harden the lib cache prune: pin the marker refresh and polish\n\n- Assert in the prune test that a successful clear refreshes the\n  .moduleLastModified marker; without this a regression that skipped\n  every marker write would pass the suite while silently turning each\n  optimized startup into a full cache wipe and re-expansion.\n- Rename the unreadable-marker test to \"unparseable\": it exercises the\n  NumberFormatException arm of the catch, not the IOException arm.\n- Extract a moduleWithTempOmod test helper for the repeated\n  module-plus-temp-omod fixture.\n- Document in deleteLibCacheFolder why a disposed classloader keeps\n  working on POSIX after the prune (unlink preserves its open jar\n  handles, unlike the previous in-place overwrite that corrupted them)\n  and that the guard refusal also returns false.\n- Align the marker read/write warning wording.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"e72a818d09b603a075ddf1040be58c9291ddb47b","date":"2026-07-08T21:31:54+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6674: List backport releases in the minutes code @since tag (#6269)","refs":"","body":"The constant landed on 2.8.x and 2.9.x after the backports merged, so\nthe tag now lists 2.8.8, 2.9.0 and 3.0.0 in the style of the existing\nmulti-release tags in OpenmrsConstants. The other constants introduced\nby TRUNK-6674 remain 3.0.0 only, since the UCUM resolution was\ndeliberately not backported.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"4d8d419630e1ff1d46616c38573f429fd3038ff8","date":"2026-07-08T20:47:03+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6674: Resolve drug order duration units across all known SNOMED CT and UCUM codes (#6246)","refs":"","body":"Saving a drug order whose duration units concept carries the current\nSNOMED CT minute code 1156209001 failed with HTTP 500. SNOMED CT\ninactivated the legacy minute code 258701004 in its 2021-07-31 release\nand dictionaries such as CIEL now map Minutes to the active code.\n\nResolve duration units deterministically from all of a concept's\nSAME-AS mappings via Duration.getDuration(Integer, Concept): SNOMED CT\nmappings take priority and UCUM strictly fills gaps, unresolvable units\nfail at validation instead of at save time, and getCode is deprecated\nwith behavior unchanged. The vocabulary registries are compiled in by\ndesign; the class Javadoc records the invariants and TRUNK-6674 records\nthe alternatives considered.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"84963803c794accceb19cf2236b859c747371336","date":"2026-07-01T13:43:53+02:00","message":"Fix @since 2.9.x to 2.9.0","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"rkorytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"},{"hash":"a6ec6555bcd71f00d07a25d2f2e8f089c4842451","date":"2026-06-30T11:29:11+02:00","message":"TRUNK-6515: Include message broker for publishing / subscribing to external events (#6205)","refs":"","body":"(cherry picked from commit bda3963b815c36dcd768d9e515024eaff7f482a4)\n","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":73}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07290e56-1d46-4e0d-b9b0-83213a0fc5c1","uuid":"9fc03937-7fd1-4e1c-9212-d0fa31f186c0","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:37:17.390Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"960f1cb95496e66ab8047a5f83eda6c1b2ecb2e2","date":"2026-08-15T02:00:17+05:30","message":"TRUNK-6717: Replace reflective BeanUtils property access with direct PersonName getters (#6431)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ranidu Nethma","authorEmail":"113999336+RaniduNethma@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"73c69ec0cea55efa51d67a8d3f19899c6eb5cf93","date":"2026-08-14T12:44:58-07:00","message":"TRUNK-6758: Remove MigrationHelper (#6457)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Idontknowthough","authorEmail":"tomlu60220244@gmail.com"},{"hash":"05bc4e4dc32c4654aba49cc76b9252def11b06c2","date":"2026-08-14T20:37:23+05:30","message":"TRUNK-6680: Restore lazy fetch semantics after JPA migration (#6379)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Mahesh5f4","authorEmail":"167050186+Mahesh5f4@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"8bb5c2e9e36ab8fb09f0053786bc0f040775cc1e","date":"2026-08-11T20:49:53+05:30","message":"TRUNK-6733: Use java-uuid-generator for entity UUIDs instead of UUID.randomUUID() (#6391)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Sathieskumar Sudeshkar","authorEmail":"sudeshkar008sk@gmail.com"},{"hash":"1b5421a9a8d69030adb91124c3f9cb758dbc58a8","date":"2026-07-24T11:14:02-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6712: Cache flattened role privileges for privilege and superuser checks (#6383)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"befcc055a108c28458fc21ff73f07dfe844f78a4","date":"2026-07-24T10:16:21-04:00","message":"Improve test suite run time (#6377)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"20b5abcfcfd8c73e0fbe40ea4586280bfff8f61e","date":"2026-07-23T13:40:47+03:00","message":"maven(deps): bump hibernateVersion from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final (#6309)","refs":"","body":"* maven(deps): bump hibernateVersion from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\n\nBumps `hibernateVersion` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final.\n\nUpdates `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-core` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/blob/7.4.5/changelog.txt)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/compare/7.3.6...7.4.5)\n\nUpdates `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-c3p0` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/blob/7.4.5/changelog.txt)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/compare/7.3.6...7.4.5)\n\nUpdates `org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-envers` from 7.3.6.Final to 7.4.5.Final\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/releases)\n- [Changelog](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/blob/7.4.5/changelog.txt)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/hibernate/hibernate-orm/compare/7.3.6...7.4.5)\n\n---\nupdated-dependencies:\n- dependency-name: org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-core\n  dependency-version: 7.4.5.Final\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n- dependency-name: org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-c3p0\n  dependency-version: 7.4.5.Final\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n- dependency-name: org.hibernate.orm:hibernate-envers\n  dependency-version: 7.4.5.Final\n  dependency-type: direct:production\n  update-type: version-update:semver-minor\n...\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\n\n* Restore primary key on order_type_class_map join table for Hibernate 7.4\n\nHibernate ORM 7.4 changed set-collection DDL generation: when a Set-based\n@ManyToMany join table declares an explicit @UniqueConstraint covering all\nof its columns, Hibernate now emits that unique constraint in place of the\ncomposite primary key it previously generated. OrderType.conceptClasses was\nthe only join table carrying such a constraint, so order_type_class_map was\ncreated without a primary key.\n\nNon-transactional integration tests build the schema via hbm2ddl and load\nstandardTestDataset.xml with dbunit's REFRESH operation, which requires a\nprimary key, so every one of them failed in setup with\nNoPrimaryKeyException: ORDER_TYPE_CLASS_MAP.\n\nThe Set's composite key already enforces the exact uniqueness the annotation\ndeclared, making uniqueConstraints redundant, and the production schema is\ndefined by Liquibase (unaffected). Removing it restores the composite primary\nkey and makes order_type_class_map consistent with the other @ManyToMany join\ntables (user_role, location_tag_map, concept_name_tag_map).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: dependabot[bot] <support@github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dependabot[bot] <49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: dkayiwa <dkayiwa@openmrs.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dependabot[bot]","authorEmail":"49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"1f6cc621cb7bf97dc4283b0c808f96373d90054f","date":"2026-07-22T15:41:22-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6711: Batch-load search result pages (#6363)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"9e011e2c09db99fd5cae20821e203fe9cc5f036b","date":"2026-07-21T23:50:01+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6681: Improve LocationSearchCriteria query performance with pagination (#6359)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"omeri innocent","authorEmail":"innocentomeri08@gmail.com"},{"hash":"265582974b2589ffc8787b57c2e4ba0368cb6cba","date":"2026-07-21T12:44:21-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6713: Follow-up: Comment clean-up","refs":"","body":"This was already included in the backports\n","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b68355b3dd934c7d5be3708d6637dfae8f845ee5","date":"2026-07-21T11:26:59-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6713: Switch to saner DaemonThread protection scheme (#6349)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"41ec2955656c6d7131c628d122d8c503b09c4cb1","date":"2026-07-21T10:37:09-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6694 & TRUNK-6695: Avoid synchronization in service fetching (#6348)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"50810cfb4d919602fa727eb78607675e2a5e3ec0","date":"2026-07-21T01:25:50+03:00","message":"Require Get Patient Programs privilege for by-uuid program lookups (#6318)","refs":"","body":"* Require Get Patient Programs privilege for by-uuid program lookups\n\nProgramWorkflowService.getPatientProgramByUuid and getPatientStateByUuid\nhad no @Authorized annotation. Because AuthorizationAdvice only enforces\nwhen a method declares a privilege, both fell through with no check at\nall, letting any authenticated user read program-enrollment PHI by uuid.\nEvery other read on the service, including getPatientProgram(Integer),\nalready requires Get Patient Programs; annotate both by-uuid methods to\nmatch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Require Get Patient Programs privilege for patient program attribute lookup\n\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName returns patient program\nattribute values keyed by patient id, yet lacked an @Authorized check.\nIts two sibling attribute readers (getPatientProgramAttributeByUuid and\ngetPatientProgramByAttributeNameAndValue) already guard on Get Patient\nPrograms, so this was a missed PHI read of the same class addressed by\nGHSA-gqf9-38mg-wgqg.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\n\n* Add authorization tests pinning the by-uuid program privilege checks\n\nThe existing tests for getPatientProgramByUuid, getPatientStateByUuid and\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName run as the privileged superuser\nand assert only find/null behavior, so they pass even if the\n@Authorized(Get Patient Programs) checks added by this branch are removed.\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName had no test at all.\n\nAdd a test per method that logs out (dropping Get Patient Programs) and\nasserts APIAuthenticationException is thrown for otherwise-valid arguments,\nmirroring AuthorizationAdviceTest and AdministrationServiceTest. These fail\nif any of the three annotations is removed, pinning the fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"f46e57d17c70440830a6ef07fde6296a79f5aed6","date":"2026-07-21T00:49:11+03:00","message":"Require allergy privileges for getAllergies and setAllergies (#6324)","refs":"","body":"* Require allergy privileges for getAllergies and setAllergies\n\nPatientService.getAllergies(Patient) and setAllergies(Patient, Allergies)\ncarried no @Authorized annotation. AuthorizationAdvice only enforces when\na method declares a privilege, so both fell through with no check at all,\nletting any authenticated caller read or modify any patient's allergy\nlist. The per-item siblings are already guarded (getAllergy and\ngetAllergyByUuid require Get Allergies; saveAllergy requires Add/Edit\nAllergies). Annotate getAllergies with Get Allergies and setAllergies with\nAdd/Edit Allergies, and add regression tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Do not transitively require Get Allergies for internal allergy reads\n\nPR #6324 added @Authorized(GET_ALLERGIES) to PatientService.getAllergies.\nTwo internal callers reach getAllergies through the AOP service proxy, so\nthey now transitively demand Get Allergies from the outer caller. This is a\nbehavior change the existing tests did not catch:\n\n- AllergyValidator reads the patient's existing allergies to reject a\n  duplicate allergen whenever a new allergy is saved (allergyId == null).\n  That runs inside saveAllergy (RequiredDataAdvice -> ValidateUtil.validate\n  -> AllergyValidator) and on the encounter-save path, so a user holding\n  only Add/Edit Allergies could no longer add an allergy.\n- PatientServiceImpl.mergeAllergies reads both patients' allergies, but\n  mergePatients is only @Authorized(EDIT_PATIENTS), so merging began to\n  require Get Allergies as well.\n\nWrap each internal read in the standard addProxyPrivilege /\nremoveProxyPrivilege idiom so the read is done on the caller's behalf\nwithout forcing the outer operation to hold Get Allergies. The interface\n@Authorized on getAllergies is left unchanged, so direct reads still\nrequire the privilege.\n\nAdd a revert-sensitive PatientServiceTest that saves a new allergy as a\nuser holding only Add Allergies (not Get Allergies); without the fix it\nfails with an APIAuthenticationException for Get Allergies raised from the\nvalidator's duplicate check.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\n\n* Run the merge workflow tests as a non-super user\n\nmergeAndRetrieveAudit now executes mergePatients as a user who holds\nonly the privileges the merge legitimately requires, with Get Allergies\ndeliberately absent, so every audit-based merge workflow test guards the\nGet Allergies proxy block in mergeAllergies: removing that block fails\nall 27 of them with \"Privileges required: Get Allergies\".\n\nRunning the merge without super-user privileges surfaced one more\ninternal read that leaked its privilege onto the caller: voiding the\nlosing patient triggers PatientDataVoidHandler, which proxies Edit\nCohorts for CohortService.notifyPatientVoided, but the membership read\ninside that method goes through the service proxy and demanded Get\nPatient Cohorts from the voiding user. That read now acquires its own\nproxy privilege, matching the allergy reads, and the test privilege set\nomits Get Patient Cohorts so both internal reads stay covered.\n\nSuggested by @ibacher during review.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"d992f1746c140dc2effaf78fc86443ac35309a3c","date":"2026-07-20T23:48:04+03:00","message":"Bind caller-supplied names as query parameters instead of concatenating (#6335)","refs":"","body":"* Bind the program-attribute name as a query parameter\n\ngetPatientProgramAttributeByAttributeName assembled its native query by\nconcatenating the attributeName argument straight into the SQL text. Bind\nit as a named parameter (:attributeName) instead so the value is always\nhandled as a literal attribute-type name and can never alter the query.\nThe patient-id list stays inlined since those elements are ints.\n\nAdds a regression test that a name containing SQL control characters is\nmatched literally and resolves no attribute type.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TpKNfxm3QjwUBDePEtFm2H\n\n* Bind the global-property name in FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue\n\nReplace the concatenated global_property lookup with a PreparedStatement\nso the property name is always treated as a literal value rather than\nbeing spliced into the SQL text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add regression test for FilterUtil.getGlobalPropertyValue name binding\n\nGuards that the property name is matched literally: a name carrying SQL\ncontrol characters resolves no property (returns null) instead of being\ninterpreted as query text, which the earlier concatenated query allowed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"c21a7cbfa2c9f67c1991372a343217e949e04f44","date":"2026-07-17T18:15:32-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6683: Skip full-text search with drugs when a concept is provided (#6346)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"375abbe5b5f9a52df6ea4cce33fc3ecdfba16c77","date":"2026-07-17T16:35:27-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6516: Follow-up: fix tests","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"11489bdb02063ff8138f45803c336b7ef4635179","date":"2026-07-17T08:26:55-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6687: Improve performance of searches using the search index (#6342)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"eb0a1006c7e188d4408deb298685c98ea1fef321","date":"2026-07-17T07:59:02-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6688: Fix circular initialization error in logging setup (#6341)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"d8fe1365fbce0b4d3fc43045dff3b69ce58ca2f4","date":"2026-07-15T16:25:59+03:00","message":"Require privileges for unprotected CohortService methods (#6317)","refs":"","body":"* Require Purge Cohorts privilege for CohortService.purgeCohort\n\npurgeCohort permanently and irreversibly removes a cohort from the\ndatabase but carried no @Authorized annotation, so any authenticated\nuser could reach it through the REST purge path\n(DELETE /ws/rest/v1/cohort/{uuid}?purge=true), even though the\nreversible voidCohort on the same resource requires Delete Cohorts.\nA dedicated Purge Cohorts privilege already exists in PrivilegeConstants\nbut was never applied. Annotate purgeCohort with it, consistent with the\nrest of the service.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add regression test for Purge Cohorts authorization\n\nGuards the @Authorized gate on CohortService.purgeCohort so that\ndropping the annotation fails the build instead of silently\nreopening the purge path to unprivileged callers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Require Get Patient Cohorts privilege for CohortService.getCohorts\n\ngetCohorts(String) was the only read on the service with no\n@Authorized, reading straight from the DAO while every sibling\ngetter requires Get Patient Cohorts. A direct service-layer caller\ncould therefore list cohorts (names, descriptions, member patient\nids) with no authorization; the REST search path was only covered\nincidentally by the resource's required-get privilege at conversion\ntime. Gate it at the service layer to match the other getters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Assert the specific privilege in cohort authorization tests\n\nCapture the thrown APIAuthenticationException and assert its message\nnames the required privilege, so a future edit that swaps either\nannotation to a different privilege (for purgeCohort, the exact\nregression this PR fixes: gating on Get Patient Cohorts instead of\nPurge Cohorts) fails the build rather than staying green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Use containsString matcher for cohort authorization assertions\n\nassertThat(msg, containsString(privilege)) reports the actual message\non failure, so a future privilege regression is self-describing in the\nCI log instead of the bare \"expected true but was false\" that\nassertTrue(msg.contains(..)) produces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"9c515246b4f37eafec0d6fc24de5b0455b9e3951","date":"2026-07-15T02:38:10+03:00","message":"mergePatients does not reassign Conditions, Allergies, or MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient (#6198) (#6315)","refs":"","body":"* mergePatients now reassigns Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses to the surviving patient\n\nPatientServiceImpl.mergePatients had no reassignment helpers for the\npatient-scoped Conditions, Allergies and MedicationDispenses tables, which\nwere added to core after the merge logic was written. After a merge these\nclinical records stayed attached to the now-voided non-preferred patient and\nsilently disappeared from the surviving patient's record - a clinical-data-loss\nand patient-safety concern (e.g. a hidden allergy).\n\nAdd mergeConditions, mergeAllergies and mergeMedicationDispenses helpers that\nmove each non-voided record from the non-preferred to the preferred patient via\nthe corresponding services, mirroring the existing\nmergeObservationsNotContainedInEncounters pattern. Saving through the services\nkeeps the changes audited and emits the normal save events. The moves are\nrecorded in new PersonMergeLogData collections so they appear in the\nPersonMergeLog.\n\nAllergies are deduplicated by allergen: an allergy whose allergen the preferred\npatient already records is not moved, because a patient cannot hold two\nallergies for the same allergen and a duplicate would make the survivor's\nallergy list fail to load afterwards.\n\nFixes #6194\n\n\n\n* Keep @since on the new PersonMergeLogData accessors only, not the private fields\n\nThe moved* fields are private (not API and not rendered by Javadoc), so the\nfield-level @since 2.9.0 tags were redundant. The public getters/adders keep\n@since 2.9.0, matching the codebase convention (Patient, Condition, Allergy\nattach @since to accessors, not backing fields).\n\n\n\n---------\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit 51422097a51a0918a9524ce8c0bd3aa76d17e25a)\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"a2d22b85955401c2d12d3ebecd9e3f483cd905e8","date":"2026-07-15T01:34:15+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6675: Module is not updated when omod changes (#6257) (#6314)","refs":"","body":"* TRUNK-6675: Module is not updated when omod changes\n\n* TRUNK-6675: Address review comments\n\n- Split the deleteDirectory try-catch in the optimized-startup branch so IOException from deletion logs an accurate message instead of \"Error while reading module last modified file\"\n- Pin getLibCacheFolderForModule_shouldRecreateNonEmptyDirWhenModuleChanged to the module-changed branch by explicitly setting optimized.startup=true\n\n\n\n* TRUNK-6675: Address review comments\n\n- Extract deleteLibCacheDir helper to reduce cognitive complexity (fixes SonarCloud quality gate)\n- Guard .moduleLastModified write on successful deletion so a failed delete does not mask the problem on the next restart\n- Fix Context.getRuntimeProperties() defensive-copy bug in both tests: mutate the copy and push it back via Context.setRuntimeProperties() so isOptimizedStartup() actually sees the change\n\n\n\n* Update api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/ModuleClassLoader.java\n\n\n\n---------\n\n\n\n(cherry picked from commit 918f05117302df56e7fb74193ffd4e4cf926d0ed)\n\nCo-authored-by: Rafal Korytkowski <rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"adec7344f655076c00cfa8ef033d998c2b8e1f5d","date":"2026-07-14T22:28:41+02:00","message":"TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6298)","refs":"","body":"* TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6289)\n\nAddresses findings 1, 2, 4, 5, 7 from the sign-off issue:\n\n- Finding 1: OutboxEventRegistry now triggers scheduler when listeners are\n  found, replacing the SmartInitializingSingleton in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer.\n  Adds registerBean() so modules can register listeners at runtime.\n- Finding 2: Use Context.loadClass() instead of Class.forName() in\n  OutboxPollingTaskHandler so module-defined event types resolve correctly.\n- Finding 4: Change outbox_event.payload and completed_listeners columns\n  from TEXT to MEDIUMTEXT in both the update changelog and schema-only snapshot;\n  align OutboxEvent entity columnDefinition to match.\n- Finding 5: BrokerEventListenerFactory now rejects BrokerIncomingEvent<?>\n  (wildcard/raw) at registration time with a clear error instead of silently\n  wiring a consumer that dead-letters every message.\n- Finding 7: Document on OpenmrsServiceEventAdvice that a synchronous\n  @EventListener exception aborting the service call is intentional.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix getMaximumPropertyLength to treat MEDIUMTEXT/TEXT/CLOB as unbounded\n\nOnly LONGTEXT was special-cased to return Integer.MAX_VALUE; MEDIUMTEXT\nand other LOB-like types fell through to column.getLength() (default 255),\ncausing ValidateUtil to reject payloads that fit the actual DB column.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix tests broken by Finding 1 and Finding 5 refactors\n\n- OutboxEventIT: afterSingletonsInstantiated() renamed to schedule()\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: raw BrokerIncomingEvent -> BrokerIncomingEvent<String>\n  to comply with the new fail-fast check for wildcard types\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix two test failures caused by Finding 4 and Finding 5 fixes\n\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: publish BrokerIncomingEvent<String> with a\n  payload so getResolvableType() resolves to the concrete generic type\n  and Spring's listener type-matching accepts it against the\n  BrokerIncomingEvent<String> method parameter.\n- HibernateAdministrationDAO: scope the MEDIUMTEXT/LONGTEXT unbounded\n  treatment to only those two explicit columnDefinition values; remove\n  CLOB since @Lob fields without columnDefinition map to CLOB in H2,\n  which would suppress the 64 KB TEXT length check in\n  BaseAttributeTypeValidatorTest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revise BrokerIncomingEvent/OutgoingEvent header docs and fix test\n\n* Address PR review comments on #6298\n\n- Restore deleteScheduledTasks() in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer and call\n  it from OutboxEventRegistry when disabled or no listeners found, so JobRunr\n  jobs don't keep firing after the last listener module is uninstalled\n- Drop registerBean(): ModuleUtil.refreshApplicationContext re-runs\n  afterSingletonsInstantiated() on module start, so module listeners are\n  picked up without any module-side call\n- Add String payloads to all three BrokerEventListenerTest events so\n  getResolvableType() resolves to BrokerIncomingEvent<String> and filter\n  tests actually exercise the source/broker filter logic\n- Add wildcard BrokerIncomingEvent<?> test case to BrokerEventListenerFactoryTest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"},{"hash":"17c7d2c4111bc928fd3d7bb90f6d767903ef032a","date":"2026-07-14T23:26:05+03:00","message":"Revert \"Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes (#6305)\" (#6312)","refs":"","body":"This reverts commit 4abaae2eebcf54375d5304d95a18c4b1e0a44cf7.","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"9533e285323873ae4ace289f2dfee0cd931d5622","date":"2026-07-14T23:05:24+03:00","message":"Clean up the module jar copy in ModuleClassLoader (#6307)","refs":"","body":"The module jar copy in getModuleUrls() managed its streams by hand and\nclosed them in a finally block that calls close() on references that are\nstill null when opening the input stream throws, relying on the\nsurrounding catch to swallow the resulting NullPointerException. Replace\nit with try-with-resources, which closes both streams in reverse order\nwith proper suppressed-exception handling and only closes the ones that\nwere actually opened.\n\nAlso drop the preceding \"if (!tmpModuleJar.exists()) createNewFile()\"\nblock: the FileOutputStream that copies into it creates the file anyway,\nso the pre-creation is redundant.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged; an IOException while copying is still caught and\nlogged.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"4abaae2eebcf54375d5304d95a18c4b1e0a44cf7","date":"2026-07-14T23:04:43+03:00","message":"Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes (#6305)","refs":"","body":"* Recursively clear a module's lib cache when the module changes\n\nModuleClassLoader.getLibCacheFolderForModule() wipes a module's lib cache\nfolder when the module file changed (or on non-optimized startup) so the\nmodule is fully re-expanded. It used File.delete(), which only removes an\nempty directory and silently no-ops on a populated one, and the return\nvalue was ignored. The cache folder always holds the module jar,\nlib/*.jar and the .moduleLastModified marker, so the delete never\nhappened.\n\nAs a result, any jar a module dropped between versions stayed in the\ncache and on the module classpath after an in-place upgrade, causing\nstale classes and version or class-identity conflicts that are hard to\ndiagnose because the omod on disk looks correct. Fresh installs are\nunaffected.\n\nReplace both delete sites with a recursive FileUtils.deleteDirectory()\nhelper, and harden the surrounding logic so a stale classpath cannot slip\nthrough silently:\n\n- If the .moduleLastModified marker cannot be read or parsed, we can no\n  longer tell whether the module changed, so clear the cache rather than\n  reuse it.\n- If the folder still cannot be fully cleared (for example a jar locked\n  by the OS during a hot reload), warn with an actionable message instead\n  of quietly expanding over the stale content.\n- Check the mkdirs() result so a cache folder that cannot be recreated is\n  visible rather than surfacing later as an obscure expansion failure.\n- Guard the recursive delete to a direct child of the lib cache root so a\n  malformed module id can never point it outside the cache.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Retry the lib cache prune on the next startup when it cannot complete\n\nTwo hardening changes to the recursive delete, from review:\n\n- getLibCacheFolderForModule no longer refreshes the .moduleLastModified\n  marker when the folder could not be fully cleared (e.g. jars still\n  locked by the previous classloader during a hot upgrade on Windows).\n  Stamping the new value over leftovers made every later optimized\n  startup trust the stale cache, so jars the delete failed to remove\n  would have stayed on the module classpath indefinitely; with a stale\n  or missing marker the next startup retries the delete once the locks\n  are gone and self-heals.\n\n- A stray regular file sitting at the cache folder's path is deleted\n  explicitly: FileUtils.deleteDirectory throws an unchecked\n  IllegalArgumentException for a non-directory, which would escape the\n  IOException catch and fail the module's startup, where the previous\n  File#delete() silently recovered.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Harden the lib cache prune: pin the marker refresh and polish\n\n- Assert in the prune test that a successful clear refreshes the\n  .moduleLastModified marker; without this a regression that skipped\n  every marker write would pass the suite while silently turning each\n  optimized startup into a full cache wipe and re-expansion.\n- Rename the unreadable-marker test to \"unparseable\": it exercises the\n  NumberFormatException arm of the catch, not the IOException arm.\n- Extract a moduleWithTempOmod test helper for the repeated\n  module-plus-temp-omod fixture.\n- Document in deleteLibCacheFolder why a disposed classloader keeps\n  working on POSIX after the prune (unlink preserves its open jar\n  handles, unlike the previous in-place overwrite that corrupted them)\n  and that the guard refusal also returns false.\n- Align the marker read/write warning wording.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"e72a818d09b603a075ddf1040be58c9291ddb47b","date":"2026-07-08T21:31:54+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6674: List backport releases in the minutes code @since tag (#6269)","refs":"","body":"The constant landed on 2.8.x and 2.9.x after the backports merged, so\nthe tag now lists 2.8.8, 2.9.0 and 3.0.0 in the style of the existing\nmulti-release tags in OpenmrsConstants. The other constants introduced\nby TRUNK-6674 remain 3.0.0 only, since the UCUM resolution was\ndeliberately not backported.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"4d8d419630e1ff1d46616c38573f429fd3038ff8","date":"2026-07-08T20:47:03+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6674: Resolve drug order duration units across all known SNOMED CT and UCUM codes (#6246)","refs":"","body":"Saving a drug order whose duration units concept carries the current\nSNOMED CT minute code 1156209001 failed with HTTP 500. SNOMED CT\ninactivated the legacy minute code 258701004 in its 2021-07-31 release\nand dictionaries such as CIEL now map Minutes to the active code.\n\nResolve duration units deterministically from all of a concept's\nSAME-AS mappings via Duration.getDuration(Integer, Concept): SNOMED CT\nmappings take priority and UCUM strictly fills gaps, unresolvable units\nfail at validation instead of at save time, and getCode is deprecated\nwith behavior unchanged. The vocabulary registries are compiled in by\ndesign; the class Javadoc records the invariants and TRUNK-6674 records\nthe alternatives considered.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"84963803c794accceb19cf2236b859c747371336","date":"2026-07-01T13:43:53+02:00","message":"Fix @since 2.9.x to 2.9.0","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"rkorytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"},{"hash":"a6ec6555bcd71f00d07a25d2f2e8f089c4842451","date":"2026-06-30T11:29:11+02:00","message":"TRUNK-6515: Include message broker for publishing / subscribing to external events (#6205)","refs":"","body":"(cherry picked from commit bda3963b815c36dcd768d9e515024eaff7f482a4)\n","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":73}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AJGrEKurdMnGDfJikgBTWd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgLN3qN1skhuYHmvXoSYR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SXqFmhjTmnQVkUfu8HgC94","name":"mcp__falkon__list_commits","input":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core","path":"api/src/main/java/org/openmrs","since":"2026-04-14","perPage":30,"page":3},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4477,"cache_read_input_tokens":20243,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4477},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07290e56-1d46-4e0d-b9b0-83213a0fc5c1","uuid":"5fe544bf-00ee-41a6-a441-c31fb2d417da","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:37:17.569Z","request_id":"req_011CgLN3q6dxWnpFv6DiNVNk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SXqFmhjTmnQVkUfu8HgC94":{"repo":"github.com/openmrs/openmrs-core","path":"api/src/main/java/org/openmrs","since":"2026-04-14","perPage":30,"page":3}},"tool_use_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SXqFmhjTmnQVkUfu8HgC94","display_name":"List Commits","server_display_name":"falkon-mcp-server","tool_name":"list_commits"}]}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SXqFmhjTmnQVkUfu8HgC94","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"c4aca3af4154dc99969cb6aed48a1e71c9a70055","date":"2026-07-01T11:17:09+02:00","message":"Porting TRUNK-6429 and TRUNK-6515 to master (#6233)","refs":"","body":"* TRUNK-6429: Create application events for service method calls and entity changes (#6084)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 144fee399f79b7152f2fcbaade069a7cfd3285e3)\n\n* TRUNK-6516: Provide CDC mechanism with Debezium (#6151)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 57f4018ffbcdb27dac86677ca2791d9fae6cfc89)\n\n* TRUNK-6429: Addressing post commit review (#6190)\n\n(cherry picked from commit a4331e297c2ad33b9d615174f7b6e52b26ef236c)","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b8e70f6a839fd77c9d396b2f40b83064d88498b2","date":"2026-06-25T00:33:14+03:00","message":"Use PipeParser for inbound HL7 to remove XML/XXE attack surface (#6223)","refs":"","body":"The hL7Parser bean was a HAPI GenericParser, which auto-detects message\nencoding and routes XML-encoded payloads to HAPI's XML parser. That XML\nparser can expose XML external entity (XXE) processing - external file\nreads, SSRF and entity-expansion DoS - when its underlying JAXP factory is\nnot hardened. OpenMRS only ever produces and consumes pipe-delimited (ER7)\nHL7v2 messages, so the XML branch is unused attack surface.\n\nSwitch the bean to a PipeParser, which rejects XML payloads outright with\nan unsupported-encoding error. The HL7ServiceImpl parser field and setter\nare widened to the common Parser supertype so injection still resolves and\nexisting setParser callers remain source-compatible.\n\nAdds a regression test asserting an XML/DOCTYPE/external-entity payload is\nrefused before any XML processing occurs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"f5c03501860de4372d7e0e12f9c3dbe025a38dc8","date":"2026-06-18T17:08:02+03:00","message":"Require Get Alerts privilege to read all users' alerts (#6186)","refs":"","body":"* Require Get Alerts privilege to read all users' alerts\n\nAlertService.getAllAlerts() and getAllAlerts(boolean) return every user's\nalerts, but were guarded only by @Authorized (authentication), so any\nauthenticated user could read alerts addressed to others through any consumer\n(REST, legacy UI, modules, direct API).\n\nIntroduce a dedicated Get Alerts privilege (following the GET_* read-privilege\nconvention) and gate both methods with it. The per-user reads (getAlerts,\ngetAlertsByUser, getAllActiveAlerts) stay open so a user can still read their\nown alerts. The privilege is created on startup via @AddOnStartup and is not\nauto-granted to any role, so this does not reintroduce the leak.\n\nAlertReminderTask reads all alerts as its configured (possibly unprivileged)\nscheduled-job user, so it grants itself a proxy Get Alerts privilege for that\nread.\n\nUpgrade note: existing roles that relied on Manage Alerts to list alerts must\nbe granted the new Get Alerts privilege (super users are unaffected).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Tighten cross-user alert reads on getAlert and getAlerts\n\ngetAllAlerts() is gated by Get Alerts, but getAlert(Integer),\ngetAlerts(User, ...), getAlertsByUser(User) and getAllActiveAlerts(User)\nstill let any authenticated caller read another user's alerts by passing\nsomeone else's id/User. Guard them in the service layer: a caller may read\ntheir own alerts, and reading another user's alerts requires the Get Alerts\nprivilege. getAlertsByUser and getAllActiveAlerts delegate through the\nguarded getAlerts; the self check compares userId, the same key the query\nfilters on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Return null from getAlert for another user's alert instead of throwing\n\ngetAlert(Integer) threw APIAuthenticationException when an alert existed but was addressed to another user, yet returned null for a non-existent id - letting an authenticated caller distinguish the two and probe which alert ids exist. It now returns null in both cases so the lookup cannot be used as an existence oracle. Reading one's own alert, and privileged reads via the Get Alerts privilege, are unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"3f5c8a66c9f3e132036cfa362aee752a8f71b263","date":"2026-06-08T09:34:16+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6558 Return null from getTaskByName when the task does not exist (#6163)","refs":"","body":"JobRunrSchedulerService.getTaskByName propagated the DAO's\nObjectRetrievalFailureException when no task matched, breaking the\nlong-standing SchedulerService contract (the pre-JobRunr\nTimerSchedulerServiceImpl caught the exception and returned null).\nModules that probe for their task before registering it - e.g.\nschedulerService.getTaskByName(NAME) == null - failed to start on any\nfresh database.\n\nRestore the historical behavior: catch ObjectRetrievalFailureException,\nlog a warning, and return null.","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"949b8a177e825320b0d04108accf38fc48751ed3","date":"2026-06-02T20:17:10+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6643: Initial setup with MariaDB Driver does not work (#6150)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"jwnasambu","authorEmail":"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"2c322bed1ac7f919fa695f68ace2f780cce9c0f4","date":"2026-06-02T10:40:38-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6392: Improvements to the OpenMRS Logging plugin (#6104)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"b3a2fa0b2d45c31065f89651f4f9801aa45354b4","date":"2026-06-01T17:21:50-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria, (#6079)","refs":"","body":"* TRUNK-6633 Add a way to search Concepts by ConceptSearchCriteria,\n\n* address feedback\n\n* add support for searching by concept name; fix test\n\n* address feedback\n\n* misc styling\n\n* change since version to 2.8.7; address feedback\n\n* add @BatchSize to ConceptReferenceTerm\n\n* switch to addUuids(String... uuids) and addConceptId(Integer... conceptIds)","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"6783feb18c2d1ede60c28af5293340cf56e0b5e8","date":"2026-06-01T12:28:57-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6647: Add @BatchSize annotation to ConceptReferenceTerm (#6149)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"8874c97439548ef26372a9bea7a275ed9881fca6","date":"2026-05-28T18:26:11+03:00","message":"Use long for offset in JobRunrSchedulerService.getTasks","refs":"","body":"JobRunr 8.6.1 changed OffsetBasedPageRequest to take (String, Long, Integer)\ninstead of (String, long, int); Java does not auto-widen-and-box int to Long,\nbreaking compilation on the bump in PR #6131. Widening the local offset field\nto long restores compatibility with both 8.5.2 and 8.6.1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"11607283d6100942c99bcdbb6713352f62c0b53a","date":"2026-05-18T12:09:40-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find … (#6088)","refs":"","body":"* TRUNK-6635 Add search by LocationSearchCriteria, with option to find descendent Locations efficiently\n\n* coderabbit suggestions\n\n* style\n\n* address feedback (with more efficient queries)\n\n* make LocationSearchCriteria take Location and LocationTag types instead of uuids\n\n* add @BatchSize to Location.tags to optimize location.getTags() calls\n\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\n\n* address feedback; change @since to 2.8.7\n\n* forward-port changes from #6089","authorName":"chibongho","authorEmail":"cbho@pih.org"},{"hash":"7590b7a4fb6c904d9cacdb0e05621ba75b6a3580","date":"2026-04-17T17:40:15-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6615:Obs setValueAsString should support standard ISO formats (apply formatter)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"mogoodrich","authorEmail":"mgoodrich@pih.org"},{"hash":"8906769730f5dc3f44c237edcc51d19f350eab80","date":"2026-04-17T17:17:11-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6615:Obs setValueAsString should support standard ISO formats (#6041)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Mark Goodrich","authorEmail":"mgoodrich@pih.org"},{"hash":"22a4bae33c93d5a235cac846a440940733a5ce42","date":"2026-04-14T14:00:17-04:00","message":"Fix admin_password_locked implementation","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":73}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07290e56-1d46-4e0d-b9b0-83213a0fc5c1","uuid":"0d546925-9c17-4f3d-b1c2-be4e524392f6","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:37:17.698Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"c4aca3af4154dc99969cb6aed48a1e71c9a70055","date":"2026-07-01T11:17:09+02:00","message":"Porting TRUNK-6429 and TRUNK-6515 to master (#6233)","refs":"","body":"* TRUNK-6429: Create application events for service method calls and entity changes (#6084)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 144fee399f79b7152f2fcbaade069a7cfd3285e3)\n\n* TRUNK-6516: Provide CDC mechanism with Debezium (#6151)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 57f4018ffbcdb27dac86677ca2791d9fae6cfc89)\n\n* TRUNK-6429: Addressing post commit review (#6190)\n\n(cherry picked from commit a4331e297c2ad33b9d615174f7b6e52b26ef236c)","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b8e70f6a839fd77c9d396b2f40b83064d88498b2","date":"2026-06-25T00:33:14+03:00","message":"Use PipeParser for inbound HL7 to remove XML/XXE attack surface (#6223)","refs":"","body":"The hL7Parser bean was a HAPI GenericParser, which auto-detect