{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WHbi3RqvGqgGY7w2t3YuBH","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"0340ada6bd4209e38630ebe7978041e0b514f85c","date":"2026-10-13T14:08:49+03:00","message":"Initialize Context's user context holder before its logger (#6672)","refs":"","body":"Fixes #6670\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f","date":"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00","message":"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"},{"hash":"83411b2f8a52325e867fccc223a54d6a6f701400","date":"2026-10-06T22:20:08+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6819: Start the JobRunr job server only once OpenMRS has started (#6654)","refs":"","body":"The background job server was started while its application context was\nstill being created, so jobs could run before the context was ready. On\njetty:run this logged \"EntityManagerFactory is closed\" for a job that ran\nduring the context refresh after modules start, against the closed session\nfactory of the context being replaced, and \"Task class ... not found\" for a\nmodule's job that ran after the first, core-only refresh, before modules\nwere loaded.\n\nThe server is now started by a SmartLifecycle once its context has finished\nrefreshing and stopped before the context closes. The webapp defers that\nstart until SchedulerService.onStartup(), which runs once modules have\nstarted; contexts refreshed after startup start their server right away.\n\nThe webapp never closes its application context, so Context.shutdown() now\ncalls SchedulerService.onShutdown() first, as it did before the move to\nJobRunr, and JobRunrSchedulerService stops the job server there, before the\nmodules and the session factory are shut down.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NK4kFG8qyevx9Bk9jWoEgS\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PdDdZrB8Q5eMgej5FmRx4R\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZ92BDLHrn6xACczVMtSiR","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"1b5421a9a8d69030adb91124c3f9cb758dbc58a8","date":"2026-07-24T11:14:02-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6712: Cache flattened role privileges for privilege and superuser checks (#6383)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"84963803c794accceb19cf2236b859c747371336","date":"2026-07-01T13:43:53+02:00","message":"Fix @since 2.9.x to 2.9.0","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"rkorytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"},{"hash":"c4aca3af4154dc99969cb6aed48a1e71c9a70055","date":"2026-07-01T11:17:09+02:00","message":"Porting TRUNK-6429 and TRUNK-6515 to master (#6233)","refs":"","body":"* TRUNK-6429: Create application events for service method calls and entity changes (#6084)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 144fee399f79b7152f2fcbaade069a7cfd3285e3)\n\n* TRUNK-6516: Provide CDC mechanism with Debezium (#6151)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 57f4018ffbcdb27dac86677ca2791d9fae6cfc89)\n\n* TRUNK-6429: Addressing post commit review (#6190)\n\n(cherry picked from commit a4331e297c2ad33b9d615174f7b6e52b26ef236c)","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":6}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07290e56-1d46-4e0d-b9b0-83213a0fc5c1","uuid":"3a86d6bd-165a-42d6-82da-0fb7db0baf61","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:37:27.632Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"0340ada6bd4209e38630ebe7978041e0b514f85c","date":"2026-10-13T14:08:49+03:00","message":"Initialize Context's user context holder before its logger (#6672)","refs":"","body":"Fixes #6670\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f","date":"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00","message":"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"},{"hash":"83411b2f8a52325e867fccc223a54d6a6f701400","date":"2026-10-06T22:20:08+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6819: Start the JobRunr job server only once OpenMRS has started (#6654)","refs":"","body":"The background job server was started while its application context was\nstill being created, so jobs could run before the context was ready. On\njetty:run this logged \"EntityManagerFactory is closed\" for a job that ran\nduring the context refresh after modules start, against the closed session\nfactory of the context being replaced, and \"Task class ... not found\" for a\nmodule's job that ran after the first, core-only refresh, before modules\nwere loaded.\n\nThe server is now started by a SmartLifecycle once its context has finished\nrefreshing and stopped before the context closes. The webapp defers that\nstart until SchedulerService.onStartup(), which runs once modules have\nstarted; contexts refreshed after startup start their server right away.\n\nThe webapp never closes its application context, so Context.shutdown() now\ncalls SchedulerService.onShutdown() first, as it did before the move to\nJobRunr, and JobRunrSchedulerService stops the job server there, before the\nmodules and the session factory are shut down.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NK4kFG8qyevx9Bk9jWoEgS\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PdDdZrB8Q5eMgej5FmRx4R\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LZ92BDLHrn6xACczVMtSiR","authorName":"dkayiwa",