{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F3B5nrGpMYRRnGHW2aqe6s","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"5eb8cba2e30befeaec8ab7892dff14ac7dcc9d87","date":"2026-10-13T17:37:18+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException (#6674)","refs":"HEAD, origin/master, origin/HEAD, master","body":"* TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException\n\nSince TRUNK-6799, AuthorizationAdvice and core's explicit privilege\nchecks denied with Spring Security's AccessDeniedException rather than\nAPIAuthenticationException. Code catching the old type stopped\nrecognizing denials; webservices.rest maps only that type, so REST\nanswered 500 where it answered 401 or 403.\n\nAPIAuthenticationException now extends AuthorizationDeniedException.\nCore throws it again wherever it did before 3.0.0, and wherever a\n@PreAuthorize or @PostAuthorize check names the missing privilege, so a\ncatch on either type recognizes the denial. It stays deprecated in\nfavour of AccessDeniedException, which every denial is.\n\nIt is no longer an APIException, so a module compiled against an earlier\ncore whose bytecode treats it as one fails verification until rebuilt.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\n\n* TRUNK-6823: Deny a failed isAuthenticated() with APIAuthenticationException too\n\n@PreAuthorize(\"isAuthenticated()\"), the migration guide's translation of a\nno-value @Authorized, denied a logged-out caller with a plain\nAuthorizationDeniedException where @Authorized throws\nAPIAuthenticationException, so converting such a method changed what its\ncallers catch. It now records the denial for\nPrivilegeNamingAuthorizationManager to report as AuthorizationAdvice does.\n\nTestInstallUtil throws APIAuthenticationException again, as before 3.0.0,\nand the migration guide notes that the class is no longer an APIException.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WMHrjRkMgotZngQzt31zSK\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"a69b14a84bf925ff7cdf34e93ca1ffb4f257265f","date":"2026-10-08T15:44:45+02:00","message":"TRUNK-6799 Introduce Spring Security with support for legacy authentication context (#6544)","refs":"","body":"Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b9993c839cf8ddf521e361970337c972d9729f7e","date":"2026-10-06T16:07:11+03:00","message":"Ensure core service advisors apply when modules declare FactoryBean services (#6631)","refs":"","body":"* Ensure core service advisors apply when modules declare FactoryBean services\n\nFixes #6630\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Fp7T1pGYEMrMVp1M7AW9Fg\n\n* Declare optimized proxies by their target class and test types before creation\n\nTransactionProxyFactoryBean definitions that set optimize get a CGLIB proxy\nof their target from Spring, so they now declare the target class, as\nproxyTargetClass ones do. The type-matching test now runs the post processor\non a bare bean factory and checks the lookups before anything is created, and\nthat they agree with the types Spring then creates, since the previous version\nstill passed with the post processor removed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01B2oUEh4gpUNZ8KRncEcwRX\n\n* Leave proxies whose target is a factory bean for Spring to type\n\nA TransactionProxyFactoryBean whose target references another factory\nbean was declared as Object, because looking up the referenced factory\nbean's type without creating it gives Object, so by-type lookups missed\nthe proxy until it was created. Such definitions are now left alone, as\ninner factory bean targets already were, and Spring determines their\ntype as before.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012oVHK8PwaoTjjKonYkfCvh\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"dkayiwa","authorEmail":"dkayiwa@openmrs.org"},{"hash":"a48d5d8a398069f34955affb6f783b79f122423a","date":"2026-09-03T16:31:56-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6698 & TRUNK-6776: Cache @Authorized metadata and add tests for class hierarchy (#6508)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"e2056c9af9036ddef415212ec8da7b0bc2eda96e","date":"2026-08-24T10:44:30-04:00","message":"TRUNK-6784: LoggingAdvice should have a fast exit path (#6488)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"adec7344f655076c00cfa8ef033d998c2b8e1f5d","date":"2026-07-14T22:28:41+02:00","message":"TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6298)","refs":"","body":"* TRUNK-6516: Fix outbox/broker issues found in events/CDC sign-off (#6289)\n\nAddresses findings 1, 2, 4, 5, 7 from the sign-off issue:\n\n- Finding 1: OutboxEventRegistry now triggers scheduler when listeners are\n  found, replacing the SmartInitializingSingleton in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer.\n  Adds registerBean() so modules can register listeners at runtime.\n- Finding 2: Use Context.loadClass() instead of Class.forName() in\n  OutboxPollingTaskHandler so module-defined event types resolve correctly.\n- Finding 4: Change outbox_event.payload and completed_listeners columns\n  from TEXT to MEDIUMTEXT in both the update changelog and schema-only snapshot;\n  align OutboxEvent entity columnDefinition to match.\n- Finding 5: BrokerEventListenerFactory now rejects BrokerIncomingEvent<?>\n  (wildcard/raw) at registration time with a clear error instead of silently\n  wiring a consumer that dead-letters every message.\n- Finding 7: Document on OpenmrsServiceEventAdvice that a synchronous\n  @EventListener exception aborting the service call is intentional.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix getMaximumPropertyLength to treat MEDIUMTEXT/TEXT/CLOB as unbounded\n\nOnly LONGTEXT was special-cased to return Integer.MAX_VALUE; MEDIUMTEXT\nand other LOB-like types fell through to column.getLength() (default 255),\ncausing ValidateUtil to reject payloads that fit the actual DB column.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix tests broken by Finding 1 and Finding 5 refactors\n\n- OutboxEventIT: afterSingletonsInstantiated() renamed to schedule()\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: raw BrokerIncomingEvent -> BrokerIncomingEvent<String>\n  to comply with the new fail-fast check for wildcard types\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix two test failures caused by Finding 4 and Finding 5 fixes\n\n- BrokerEventListenerTest: publish BrokerIncomingEvent<String> with a\n  payload so getResolvableType() resolves to the concrete generic type\n  and Spring's listener type-matching accepts it against the\n  BrokerIncomingEvent<String> method parameter.\n- HibernateAdministrationDAO: scope the MEDIUMTEXT/LONGTEXT unbounded\n  treatment to only those two explicit columnDefinition values; remove\n  CLOB since @Lob fields without columnDefinition map to CLOB in H2,\n  which would suppress the 64 KB TEXT length check in\n  BaseAttributeTypeValidatorTest.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Revise BrokerIncomingEvent/OutgoingEvent header docs and fix test\n\n* Address PR review comments on #6298\n\n- Restore deleteScheduledTasks() in OutboxTaskSchedulerInitializer and call\n  it from OutboxEventRegistry when disabled or no listeners found, so JobRunr\n  jobs don't keep firing after the last listener module is uninstalled\n- Drop registerBean(): ModuleUtil.refreshApplicationContext re-runs\n  afterSingletonsInstantiated() on module start, so module listeners are\n  picked up without any module-side call\n- Add String payloads to all three BrokerEventListenerTest events so\n  getResolvableType() resolves to BrokerIncomingEvent<String> and filter\n  tests actually exercise the source/broker filter logic\n- Add wildcard BrokerIncomingEvent<?> test case to BrokerEventListenerFactoryTest\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"},{"hash":"c4aca3af4154dc99969cb6aed48a1e71c9a70055","date":"2026-07-01T11:17:09+02:00","message":"Porting TRUNK-6429 and TRUNK-6515 to master (#6233)","refs":"","body":"* TRUNK-6429: Create application events for service method calls and entity changes (#6084)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 144fee399f79b7152f2fcbaade069a7cfd3285e3)\n\n* TRUNK-6516: Provide CDC mechanism with Debezium (#6151)\n\n(cherry picked from commit 57f4018ffbcdb27dac86677ca2791d9fae6cfc89)\n\n* TRUNK-6429: Addressing post commit review (#6190)\n\n(cherry picked from commit a4331e297c2ad33b9d615174f7b6e52b26ef236c)","authorName":"Rafal Korytkowski","authorEmail":"rafal.korytkowski@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":7}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07290e56-1d46-4e0d-b9b0-83213a0fc5c1","uuid":"dbdb5310-457a-4c23-b0d0-daae1f9fec5c","timestamp":"2026-10-24T03:38:42.547Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"5eb8cba2e30befeaec8ab7892dff14ac7dcc9d87","date":"2026-10-13T17:37:18+03:00","message":"TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an AuthorizationDeniedException (#6674)","refs":"HEAD, origin/master, origin/HEAD, master","body":"* TRUNK-6823: Deny with APIAuthenticationException again, as an Authoriz